<title>HONG KONG: Goodwill 1996 profit rises 46.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Goodwill 1996 profit rises 46.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 33.8   vs  37.4 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  5.0    vs  8.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			  92.65  vs  63.15</p>
<p>    Turnover		   786.15 vs  510.59</p>
<p>    Company name	     Goodwill Investment (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		April 28 to May 5</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 May 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Goodwill is a property investment and development and financial services firm.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-two shares held.</p>
<p>The calculation of share earnings is based on the weighted average of 274 million shares vs 168 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs eight cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
